In article <1990Dec2.192636.3897@aplcen.apl.jhu.edu>, theune@aplcen.apl.jhu.edu (Peter Theune) writes...
>Okay, so how do I get into wizard mode . I've tried the -D flag, my name
>is compiled in, I tried both uppercase and quoted lowercase. All to no
>avail. Any help would be appreciated.

     The VMS username--not any user-specifiable player name--should be
in uppercase, as the comment in vmsconf.h indicates.  The default value
"GENTZEL" :-) is in the proper format.  The command line switch must also
be in uppercase.  Since NetHack is written in C, and the C startup code
converts unquoted text into lowercase, you must quote "-D".  Either of
the following should work:
|$ nethack "-D"
or
|$ nethack -"D"

     If you're using a DCL command procedure to start the program, make
sure that it passes _its_ command line arguments to the NetHack invocation
and that it preserves quoting.  (Perhaps something like
|$ mcr hackdir:nethack "''p1'" "''p2'"
with up to eight quoted arguments.)

